To compute its Tate resolution on the ambient space P^2 \times P^2, we first
consider it as a sheaf on P^2 \times P^2, and then take a linear presentation
matrix via a truncation.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i33 : phi = map(SX,S,vars SX);              |
|                                            |
|o33 : RingMap SX <-- S                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i34 : betti (L=prune pushForward(phi,LX))   |
|                                            |
|              0  1                          |
|o34 = total: 10 27                          |
|          0:  1  .                          |
|          1:  1  1                          |
|          2:  .  1                          |
|          3:  8 25                          |
|                                            |
|o34 : BettiTally                            |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i35 : Ltr = (truncate ({2,2},L))**S^{{2,2}};|
+--------------------------------------------+
|i36 : betti freeResolution Ltr              |
|                                            |
|              0   1   2  3  4               |
|o36 = total: 60 176 184 80 12               |
|          0: 60 176 184 80 12               |
