beilinson -- apply the beilinson functor
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        M=beilinson F
        phi=beilinson psi
        C=beilinson T
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a free module over the
        exterior algebra E
      * psi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a map between free modules
        over E
      * T, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a complex of free modules over
        E
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BundleType => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value
        PrunedQuotient, the possible values are described in BundleType
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a module over the symmetric
        algebra S
      * phi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a map between S-modules
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a chain complex of S-modules

Description
===========

The Beilinson functor is a functor from the category of free E-modules to the
category of coherent sheaves which associates to a cyclic free E-module of
generated in multidegree a the vector bundle U^a. Note that the U^a for
multidegrees a=\{a_1,...,a_t\} with 0 \le a_i \le n_i form a full exceptional
series for the derived category of coherent sheaves on the product PP = P^{n_1}
\times ... \times P^{n_t} of t projective spaces, see e.g. Tate Resolutions on
Products of Projective Spaces (see http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.5724 ).

In the function we compute from a complex of free E-modules the corresponding
complex of graded S-modules, whose sheafifications are the corresponding
sheaves. The corresponding graded S-module are chosen as quotients of free
S-modules in case of the default option BundleType=>PrunedQuotient, or as
submodules of free S-modules. The true Beilinson functor is obtained by the
sheafication of resulting the complex.

The Beilinson monad of a coherent sheaf $\mathcal F$ is the sheafication of
beilinson( T($\mathcal F$)) of its Tate resolution T($\mathcal F$).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces {2,1}                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = (S, E)                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : psi=random(E^{{-1,0}}, E^{{-2,-1}})                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {1, 0} | 107e_(0,0)e_(1,0)-5570e_(0,1)e_(1,0)+3783e_(0,2)e_(1,0)+4376e_(|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     0,0)e_(1,1)+3187e_(0,1)e_(1,1)-5307e_(0,2)e_(1,1) |                     |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix E  <-- E                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : phi=beilinson psi                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {1, 0} | -5307x_(1,0)-3783x_(1,1) |                                     |
|     {1, 0} | -3187x_(1,0)-5570x_(1,1) |                                     |
|     {1, 0} | 4376x_(1,0)-107x_(1,1)   |                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Matrix                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : beilinson(E^{{-1,0}})                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = cokernel {1, 0} | x_(0,2)  |                                            |
|              {1, 0} | -x_(0,1) |                                            |
|              {1, 0} | x_(0,0)  |                                            |
|                                                                             |
|                            3                                                |
|o4 : S-module, quotient of S                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = complex{psi}                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|      1      1                                                               |
|o5 = E  <-- E                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : C = beilinson T                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|                                       1                                     |
|o6 = cokernel {1, 0} | x_(0,2)  | <-- S                                      |
|              {1, 0} | -x_(0,1) |                                            |
|              {1, 0} | x_(0,0)  |     1                                      |
|                                                                             |
|     0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : betti T                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1                                                              |
|o7 = total: 1 1                                                              |
|         1: 1 .                                                              |
|         2: . 1                                                              |
|                                                                             |
