beilinsonContraction -- compute a Beilinson contraction
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        beilinsonContraction(e, rowdeg, coldeg)
  * Inputs:
      * e, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of the
        exterior algebra E
      * rowdeg, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * coldeg, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, two multidegrees
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BundleType => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value
        PrunedQuotient, with values PrunedQuotient or SubBundle
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a map between modules over the
        symmetric algebra S

Description
===========

Returns a map between two Beilinson generators (i.e. the beilinson generators
beilinsonBundle(a, E) of the derived category). Note:

(1) (S,E) is the result of productOfProjectiveSpaces

(2) e is a homogeneous element of E giving a map from E(-coldeg) -->
E(-rowdeg).







+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces {2,1}                         |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = (S, E)                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o1 : Sequence                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : gens S, gens E                                                  |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = ({x   , x   , x   , x   , x   }, {e   , e   , e   , e   , e   })|
|        0,0   0,1   0,2   1,0   1,1     0,0   0,1   0,2   1,0   1,1  |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Sequence                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f=e_(0,0)*e_(0,1)*e_(1,0)                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = e   e   e                                                       |
|      0,0 0,1 1,0                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : E                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : beilinsonContraction(f,{0,0},{2,1})                             |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = | x_(0,2)x_(1,1) |                                              |
|                                                                     |
|             1      1                                                |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : m=beilinsonContraction(e_(0,0)*e_(1,0),{0,0},{1,1})             |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = | x_(0,1)x_(1,1) x_(0,2)x_(1,1) 0 |                             |
|                                                                     |
|             1      3                                                |
|o5 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

E is positively graded, in contrast to the paper!

