bgg -- make a linear free complex from a module over an exterior algebra or a symmetric algebra
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        LP = bgg P
        RM = bgg(M,LengthLimit=>4)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module over an exterior
        algebra E
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module over an symmetric
        algebra S
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * LengthLimit => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * LP, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, over a symmetric algebra
      * RM, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, over a exterior algebra

Description
===========

If P is an E-module, then LP becomes a linear complex of free S-modules, where
(S,E) is the Koszul pair corresponding to a product of projective spaces.
Similarly, if M is an S-module, them RM becomes a linear free complex over the
exterior algebra E of length bounded by the LengthLimit.

The complex LP is that produced from P by the Bernstein-Gel'fand-Gel'fand
functor called L in our paper Tate Resolutions on Products of Projective Spaces
(see http://arxiv.org/abs/ ). Similarly, the complex RM produced from M is a
bounded piece of the infinite complex of the Bernstein-Gel'fand-Gel'fand
functor called R in loc.cit. L and R form a pair of adjoint functors.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces{1,2}                          |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = (S, E)                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o1 : Sequence                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = prune truncate({1,2},E^1)**E^{{1,2}};                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : LP = bgg P                                                      |
|                                                                     |
|      1      5      6                                                |
|o3 = S  <-- S  <-- S                                                 |
|                                                                     |
|     -2     -1     0                                                 |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : Complex                                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : netList apply(toList(min LP..max LP), i-> decompose ann HH_i LP)|
|                                                                     |
|     +------------------------------------+------------------------+ |
|o4 = |ideal (x   , x   , x   , x   , x   )|                        | |
|     |        1,2   1,1   1,0   0,1   0,0 |                        | |
|     +------------------------------------+------------------------+ |
|     |ideal (x   , x   )                  |ideal (x   , x   , x   )| |
|     |        0,1   0,0                   |        1,2   1,1   1,0 | |
|     +------------------------------------+------------------------+ |
|     |ideal ()                            |                        | |
|     +------------------------------------+------------------------+ |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = prune HH_0 LP                                               |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = cokernel {1, 1} | -x_(1,2) |                                    |
|              {1, 1} | x_(1,0)  |                                    |
|              {1, 1} | -x_(1,1) |                                    |
|                                                                     |
|                            3                                        |
|o5 : S-module, quotient of S                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : betti freeResolution M                                          |
|                                                                     |
|            0 1                                                      |
|o6 = total: 3 1                                                      |
|         2: 3 1                                                      |
|                                                                     |
|o6 : BettiTally                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : high = {3,3}                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|o7 = {3, 3}                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o7 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : cohomologyMatrix(M, -high, high)                                |
|                                                                     |
|o8 = | 45h 30h 15h 0 15  30  45  |                                   |
|     | 24h 16h 8h  0 8   16  24  |                                   |
|     | 9h  6h  3h  0 3   6   9   |                                   |
|     | 0   0   0   0 0   0   0   |                                   |
|     | 3h2 2h2 h2  0 h   2h  3h  |                                   |
|     | 0   0   0   0 0   0   0   |                                   |
|     | 9h3 6h3 3h3 0 3h2 6h2 9h2 |                                   |
|                                                                     |
|                      7               7                              |
|o8 : Matrix (ZZ[h, k])  <-- (ZZ[h, k])                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : M=module ideal vars S                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = image | x_(0,0) x_(0,1) x_(1,0) x_(1,1) x_(1,2) |                       |
|                                                                             |
|                             1                                               |
|o9 : S-module, submodule of S                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : RM = bgg(M,LengthLimit=>3)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|       70      35      15      5                                             |
|o10 = E   <-- E   <-- E   <-- E                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      -4      -3      -2      -1                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : Complex                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : betti RM                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             -4 -3 -2 -1                                                     |
|o11 = total: 70 35 15  5                                                     |
|          0: 70 35 15  5                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : BettiTally                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
