coarseMultigradedRegularity -- A truncation that has linear resolution
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        R = coarseMultigradedRegularity M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, multi-graded module over a
        multi-graded polynomial ring
      * M, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, multi-graded module over a
        multi-graded polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "MinimalResolution"
  * Outputs:
      * R, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, degree such that truncate(R,M)
        has linear resolution

Description
===========

Uses a free resolution and takes the maximum degree of the terms.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces{1,1,2}    |
|                                                 |
|o1 = (S, E)                                      |
|                                                 |
|o1 : Sequence                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_(0,0)^2,x_(1,0)^3,x_(2,0)^4)    |
|                                                 |
|             2     3     4                       |
|o2 = ideal (x   , x   , x   )                    |
|             0,0   1,0   2,0                     |
|                                                 |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = coarseMultigradedRegularity(S^1/I)      |
|                                                 |
|o3 = {2, 3, 4}                                   |
|                                                 |
|o3 : List                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : N = truncate(R,S^1/I);                      |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : betti freeResolution N                      |
|                                                 |
|             0   1   2   3  4                    |
|o5 = total: 84 312 432 264 60                    |
|         9: 84 312 432 264 60                    |
|                                                 |
|o5 : BettiTally                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : netList toList tallyDegrees freeResolution N|
|                                                 |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
|o6 = |Tally{{2, 3, 4} => 84} |                   |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
|     |Tally{{2, 3, 5} => 144}|                   |
|     |      {2, 4, 4} => 84  |                   |
|     |      {3, 3, 4} => 84  |                   |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
|     |Tally{{2, 3, 6} => 60 }|                   |
|     |      {2, 4, 5} => 144 |                   |
|     |      {3, 3, 5} => 144 |                   |
|     |      {3, 4, 4} => 84  |                   |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
|     |Tally{{2, 4, 6} => 60 }|                   |
|     |      {3, 3, 6} => 60  |                   |
|     |      {3, 4, 5} => 144 |                   |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
|     |Tally{{3, 4, 6} => 60} |                   |
|     +-----------------------+                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+

See the proof of Proposition 2.7 in Tate Resolutions on Products of Projective
