+-------------------------------------------+

As a second example, consider the structure sheaf $\mathcal O_E$ of a
nonsingular cubic contained in (point)xP^2. The corresponding graded module is

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M = S^1/ideal(x_(0,0), x_(1,0)^3+x_(1,1)^3+x_(1,2)^3)|
|                                                          |
|o6 = cokernel | x_(0,0) x_(1,0)^3+x_(1,1)^3+x_(1,2)^3 |   |
|                                                          |
|                            1                             |
|o6 : S-module, quotient of S                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : low = {-3,-3};high={0,0};                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : cohomologyMatrix(M,low,high)                         |
|                                                          |
|o9 = | h+1 h+1 h+1 h+1 |                                  |
|     | 3h  3h  3h  3h  |                                  |
|     | 6h  6h  6h  6h  |                                  |
|     | 9h  9h  9h  9h  |                                  |
|                                                          |
|                      4               4                   |
|o9 : Matrix (ZZ[h, k])  <-- (ZZ[h, k])                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

and the "1+h" in the Northeast (= upper right) corner signifies that that
$h^0(\mathcal O_E) = h^1(\mathcal O_E) = 1.$

