We conclude that the sheaf represented by R0 is O(5)+O(4) on P^1, which is
correct because N represents phi^*O(1) and phi_* O_X(H) = O(2)+O(1).

Caveat
======

Note that the resulting complex is a chain complex instead of a cochain
complex, so that for example HH^i RpiM = HH_{-i} RpiM.



