isIsomorphicStrict -- probabilistic test for homogeneous isomorphism
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        v = isIsomorphicStrict(A,B)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * B, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * v, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This is the same as *note isIsomorphic: (Isomorphism)isIsomorphic, but with
additional options Strict => true and Homogeneous => true added by default.

First checks that the generator degrees are the same. Then computes a random
degree 0 map A --> B and B --> A, and returns true iff both are surjections.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/11[a,b]                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker random(S^{-2,0,1,2}, S^{3:-3})                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = cokernel {2}  | -3a-4b                         a-3b                     |
|              {0}  | 3a3-3a2b-4ab2+2b3              3a3-3a2b-3ab2+3b3        |
|              {-1} | 3a4-a3b+3a2b2-2ab3-5b4         -5a4-5a3b-4a2b2-5ab3     |
|              {-2} | -5a5+5a4b+5a3b2-2a2b3+5ab4+3b5 -2a5-5a4b-4a3b2+4a2b3+b5 |
|                                                                             |
|                            4                                                |
|o2 : S-module, quotient of S                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3a-b                         |                                               |
|-4a3+5a2b+5ab2-5b3           |                                               |
|-3a4-2a3b-5a2b2+2ab3+2b4     |                                               |
|3a5+3a4b-4a3b2-a2b3+4ab4-3b5 |                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = coker (random(cover M, cover M)*presentation M)                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = cokernel {2}  | -5a-3b                        -2a-5b                    |
|              {0}  | -2a3-2a2b-2ab2                a3-2a2b-4ab2-4b3          |
|              {-1} | -4a4-3a3b-3a2b2-3ab3+4b4      4a4+4a3b-3a2b2+5ab3+2b4   |
|              {-2} | -a5-2a4b-2a3b2+4a2b3-2ab4-4b5 3a5+a4b-4a3b2+5a2b3-3ab4  |
|                                                                             |
|                            4                                                |
|o3 : S-module, quotient of S                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|5a+2b                         |                                              |
|a3+3a2b-5ab2                  |                                              |
|-3a4-2a3b-3ab3-5b4            |                                              |
|2a5-4a4b+3a3b2-5a2b3+3ab4+5b5 |                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : tally apply(100, j->isIsomorphicStrict(M,N))                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Tally{true => 100}                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Tally                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

If the function returns true then the modules ARE isomorphic. But if it returns
false they may be isomorphic anyway.

