regionComplex -- region complex
*******************************

  * Usage: 
        regionComplex(T,c,IJK)
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, over the exterior algebra
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a (multi) degree
      * IJK, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, a sequence (I,J,K) of
        disjoint subsets of \{0..t-1\}
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a region complex of T

Description
===========

We compute the region complex of T as defined in Tate Resolutions on Products
of Projective Spaces (see http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.5724 ) section 3. Note that
different from the paper I,J,K are sublists of 0...t-1 and not subsets of 1..t.
In the examples below, only rT2 and rT3 are proper region complexes.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n={1,1};                                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
