tateExtension -- extend the terms in the Beilinson window to a part of a corner complex of the corresponding Tate resolution
****************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        T=tateExtension W
  * Inputs:
      * W, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, terms in the Beilinson window
        of a Tate resolution
  * Outputs:
      * T, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a corner complex of the
        corresponding Tate resolution

Description
===========

Every object F in the derived category D^d(P) of coherent sheaves on a product
P=P^{n_1}x..xP^{n_t} of t projective space is of the form U(W) with W a complex
with terms in the Beilinson range only. The function computes with the
algorithm (not!) described in section 4 of Tate Resolutions on Products of
Projective Spaces (see http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.5724 ) computes part of a
suitable chosen corner complex of the Tate resolution T(F).



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n={1,1};                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces n;                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T1 = (dual freeResolution(trim (ideal vars E)^2, LengthLimit => 5))[1]; |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : a=-{2,2};                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T2=(T1**E^{a})[sum a];                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
